    "hypothesis": "Scale the horizontal position, altitude, horizontal velocity, vertical velocity, and angular velocity observations to make the lander appear farther from the pad, higher, falling faster, and more tilted, prompting earlier side‑engine corrections and earlier main‑engine braking. Add a +0.5 bias to the main‑engine logit and a +0.15 bias to each side‑engine logit to compensate for the weaker main thrust while preserving stability under nominal physics.",
